@Stypox 
Thank you for the review 😄 

I rebased the complete branch and applied the requested changes.

> Okay let's come to an agreement here: I will make the text a bit larger.

@litetex I feel the need to clarify this: I'm not saying "this is what it must look like in the final release, do it my way". I'm looking to test different variations of the concept so that the final product makes the most sense. I just want to see if what I'm visualising in my head matches what it would look like in the app. Even a screenshot would be fine. 

Meanwhile, I discovered an actual issue with the placement of the seek time below the preview thumbnail. My finger covers the seek time entirely when I'm dragging it across the seekbar. I need to drag to grab the seek thumb, drag up my finger away from the seekbar, and then do the actual seeking, to be able to see the seek time. That's weird, isn't it? It forces the user to adopt a weird 'horizontal-then-vertical-then-horizontal' finger-dragging gesture technique.

@opusforlife2 @litetex Placing the seek time below the thumbnail looks more natural in my opinion, maybe just because that's the usual way. On the other hand placing the seek time above has multiple advantages: making the text more readable and having the thumbnail overlay cover a smaller portion of the player below. So I'd go with seek time above, at the end of the day.

> Though I do think it would look better with that shadow extended to the width of the thumbnail.

I'd rather not do this as it would cover more of the player below. It looks just fine as it already is imo.
